"""Editorial question designs for traditional sports, martial arts history, and archery culture."""

from review_angle_plans import audit, revise_domain


TRADITIONAL_SPORTS = """history_origins|The Early Record of a Sport|What dated evidence describes one community sport?|Separate first surviving account from invention.
famous_examples|A Celebrated Match in Context|What does one well-known event reveal about actual play?|Compare rules, competitors, setting, and later retellings.
hidden_stories|Who Sustains the Sport|Which coaches, makers, officials, and volunteers are overlooked?|Credit work and community organizing with consent.
beginner_explainers|How One Local Sport Works|What rules and aims must a newcomer understand?|Name place, governing body, equipment, and variant.
advanced_concepts|Tradition and Standard Rules|What changes when local play becomes a formal competition?|Compare rule sets, access, training, and community meaning.
mysteries_unsolved_cases|A Disputed Sport Origin|Which routes of exchange are supported by evidence?|Compare dated descriptions and avoid origin by resemblance.
technology_innovation|Equipment Change Tested|Did a new material alter performance or access?|Compare specifications, cost, safety, and player accounts.
people_personalities|An Athlete-Teacher's Contribution|How did one practitioner transmit skills?|Use dated records and credit a wider teaching network.
major_events|A Rule Change or Venue Loss|How did one event alter participation?|Trace dates, membership, access, and unintended effects.
how_it_works|A Match from Start to Finish|How are turns, scoring, officials, and disputes handled?|Document a named version and current rule source.
rise_fall|Participation Over Time|What explains a claimed revival or decline?|Check counting, informal play, facilities, and funding.
then_vs_now|The Sport Across Two Eras|How did rules, equipment, and participation change?|Use comparable sources and distinguish practice from promotion.
future_developments|Paths for Continued Play|Which resources do participants prioritize?|Compare space, coaching, equipment, safety, and governance.
myths_vs_facts|An Unchanged Ancient Sport?|Which features are documented early and which came later?|Date rules, objects, and records without authenticity ranking.
documentary_stories|One Competition Day|How do players and organizers make an event work?|Use consented observation and sourced event records.
map_vs_ground|Where Play Actually Happens|Does the official venue map reflect usable access?|Check grounds, transport, facilities, and current permissions.
route_choices|Reaching Practice|How does travel affect who can participate?|Compare time, cost, seasonal service, and access needs.
seasonality|Sport Across Seasons|How do weather and calendars shape play?|Use local schedules and dated conditions.
local_voice|Players and Neighbors|How do communities value or contest a play space?|Seek varied consented views and land-use context.
landscape_process|Terrain as Part of Play|How does one sport use a river, field, slope, or surface?|Describe the site and environmental change without assuming universality.
accessibility|Who Can Join|Which physical, sensory, cost, or social barriers exist?|Test adaptations with players rather than prescribing them.
infrastructure|Maintaining the Venue|What facilities and labor keep play possible?|Trace maintenance, funding, ownership, and access.
environmental_pressure|Impact of a Sporting Event|What resource or habitat effects can be measured?|Define attendance, travel, site condition, and baseline.
safety_decision|Current Event Conditions|Which organizer or authority notices affect participation?|Check venue, weather, equipment, and rules for the event date.
place_history|The Ground Before the Sport|How was the playing site used earlier?|Use land records and community histories.
comparison_of_places|Two Communities, Different Access|Why can one group sustain play more easily?|Compare venues, cost, coaching, rules, and participation.
responsible_access|Sharing the Playing Space|How are player needs balanced with other users?|Check rights, schedules, noise, and local agreements.
field_training_method|Learning One Skill|What sequence do coaches actually teach?|Observe consentfully and avoid unverified performance claims.
field_equipment_design|One Piece of Gear|How do material and dimensions affect use?|Compare maker intent, rules, cost, and repair.
field_rules_and_fairness|A Disputed Call|How do local and formal rules resolve it?|Use current rule text and attributed participant accounts.
field_injury_prevention|Safety Practice in Context|Which measures do organizers use and what evidence supports them?|Use sport-specific current guidance; avoid personal medical advice.
field_event_logistics|Running a Match|What staffing, venue, transport, and contingency are required?|Trace one dated event plan and actual outcome.
"""

